// `check_sound`, being built (docs/language/ownership-design.md §15.4,
// §21.4, §23; issues/ownership-checker.md item 3): the run agrees with the
// meaning wherever the checker's verdict holds. Ownership is the licence for
// the run to share; no separation algebra is used.
//
// The proof holds, so far (across the modules below):
//
// - **Selections composed**: a read, a write and a fit along an appended
//   path (`Sel::read_append`, `Sel::write_append`, `Sel::fit_append`), and a
//   place's steps as selections at the words (`Steps::read_sels`,
//   `Steps::write_sels`).
// - **Levels**: the state's levels name the environments' slots
//   (`CSt::lvl_var`, `CSt::lvl_below`), and a push keeps every earlier level
//   (`CSt::var_push`, `CSt::lvl_push_loc`).
// - **The invariant's first part** (`Sim`): each variable's run-time cell
//   agrees with the meaning's value as the checker's role says (a plain
//   variable holds the value; a holder or a view reads it through the heap,
//   its block live, its selections fitting), with `Sim::push`, the one lemma
//   every binding statement uses.
// - **Reads**: what reads a value at no selections reads its selections
//   further on where they fit (`Value::get_more`), and a place whose codes
//   have parts and whose accessors' residuals hold fits
//   (`Place::fit_from`, from `pre_inside`: `Dyn::fits_of_pre`).
// - **A read's verdict** (`ReadInv`, `CSt::read_inv`): what the checker's
//   read of a place found, split into its parts once.
// - **Stages** (`Stepped`): one lemma per statement kind, from a state the
//   invariant holds of to the next (`Stmt::stage_lit`, `Stmt::stage_op`,
//   `Stmt::stage_read`).
// - **Words**: an atom the checker reads at plain levels reads one index in
//   the run and in the meaning (`Sim::atom_ix`), and so a place's steps make
//   one list of selections in both (`Sim::steps_same`); and so the run reads
//   a place the checker read at the meaning's value (`Sim::place`), the
//   `Read` stage (`Stmt::stage_read`).
// - **The invariant** (`Inv`), its clauses explained where it is stated, and
//   the facts its entry needs (`Slot`, `Value::get_of_read`).
//
// **The modules** (split mechanically from this file, no statement changed;
// issues/ownership-sound-consolidate.md). Each imports the ones above it; a
// declaration sits in the earliest module its kind and its dependencies allow:
//
// - `sound_paths`: selections and lens laws, codes along a place, steps and
//   apartness of paths, list and Boolean lemmas: nothing of the checker's
//   state, the machine or the invariant.
// - `sound_state`: the checker's state alone: levels, ancestry, the
//   licence's decider on regions, roles and entries.
// - `sound_heap`: heaps and the frame, the run's own lemmas (`Stmt::Continues`
//   and the statement runs), cells against values (`Cell::Agrees`, `Slot`).
// - `sound_inv`: `Sim` and `Inv`, the entry, and the builders (push, gone,
//   kill, view, take).
// - `sound_write`: the writes, the write-back, the patch along chains.
// - `sound_stages`: `Stepped` and one stage per statement kind.
// - `sound_like`: `Like` and its steps.
// - `sound_ret`: the return (`Body::stage_ret`).
// - `sound_call`: the call, in parts (P1–P4).
//
// The restatement (design §26), beside the present invariant until it covers
// what that covers:
//
// - `sound_wf`: the checker's state well formed (`CSt::Wf`), the clauses
//   that read the state alone.
// - `sound_local`: the restated invariant (`InvLocal`: agreement outside
//   write children, sync, where cells live, footprints, like-ness, the heap
//   group) as definitions, with deciders (`InvLocal::holds_b`).
// - `sound_trace`: the checker, the meaning and the run stepped together and
//   a decider evaluated at every state (`Body::trace_with`).
//
// This module imports them all; it holds no declarations of its own.
import logic;
import bool;
import nat;
import option;
import list;
import bitvec;
import bitvec_nat;
import span_set;
import store;
import atom;
import steps;
import shape;
import body;
import level2;
import run;
import verdict;
import checker;
import linux_world;
import sound_paths;
import sound_state;
import sound_heap;
import sound_inv;
import sound_write;
import sound_stages;
import sound_like;
import sound_ret;
import sound_call;
import sound_wf;
import sound_local;
import sound_trace;
